{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-job-024",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 24,
  "title": "Job 24",
  "display_title": "Job 24",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "job",
  "book": "Job",
  "bookName": "Job",
  "bookOrder": 18,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 24,
  "sortOrder": 18024,
  "verseCount": 25,
  "aliases": [
    "Job"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:24:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Why, seeing times are not hidden from the Almighty, do they that know him not see his days?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 24:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:24:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:24:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Some remove the landmarks; they violently take away flocks, and feed thereof.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 24:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:24:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:24:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "They drive away the ass of the fatherless, they take the widow’s ox for a pledge.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 24:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:24:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:24:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "They turn the needy out of the way: the poor of the earth hide themselves together.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 24:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:24:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:24:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Behold, as wild asses in the desert, go they forth to their work; rising betimes for a prey: the wilderness yieldeth food for them and for their children.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 24:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:24:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:24:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "They reap every one his corn in the field: and they gather the vintage of the wicked.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 24:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:24:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:24:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "They cause the naked to lodge without clothing, that they have no covering in the cold.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 24:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:24:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:24:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "They are wet with the showers of the mountains, and embrace the rock for want of a shelter.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 24:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:24:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:24:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "They pluck the fatherless from the breast, and take a pledge of the poor.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 24:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:24:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:24:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "They cause him to go naked without clothing, and they take away the sheaf from the hungry;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 24:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:24:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:24:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Which make oil within their walls, and tread their winepresses, and suffer thirst.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 24:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:24:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:24:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Men groan from out of the city, and the soul of the wounded crieth out: yet God layeth not folly to them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 24:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:24:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:24:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "They are of those that rebel against the light; they know not the ways thereof, nor abide in the paths thereof.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 24:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:24:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:24:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "The murderer rising with the light killeth the poor and needy, and in the night is as a thief.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 24:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:24:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:24:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "The eye also of the adulterer waiteth for the twilight, saying, No eye shall see me: and disguiseth his face.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 24:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:24:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:24:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "In the dark they dig through houses, which they had marked for themselves in the daytime: they know not the light.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 24:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:24:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:24:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "For the morning is to them even as the shadow of death: if one know them, they are in the terrors of the shadow of death.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 24:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:24:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:24:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "He is swift as the waters; their portion is cursed in the earth: he beholdeth not the way of the vineyards.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 24:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:24:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:24:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "Drought and heat consume the snow waters: so doth the grave those which have sinned.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 24:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:24:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:24:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "The womb shall forget him; the worm shall feed sweetly on him; he shall be no more remembered; and wickedness shall be broken as a tree.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 24:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:24:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:24:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "He evil entreateth the barren that beareth not: and doeth not good to the widow.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 24:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:24:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:24:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "He draweth also the mighty with his power: he riseth up, and no man is sure of life.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 24:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:24:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:24:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "Though it be given him to be in safety, whereon he resteth; yet his eyes are upon their ways.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 24:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:24:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:24:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "They are exalted for a little while, but are gone and brought low; they are taken out of the way as all other, and cut off as the tops of the ears of corn.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 24:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:24:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:24:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "And if it be not so now, who will make me a liar, and make my speech nothing worth?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 24:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:24:25"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
